  "title": "Cached gate results and stored handles are reused without checking the commit they ran on",
  "file": "src/pipeline/gate-execution.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "If the checked-out commit changes between the moment a gate result is saved and the moment the daemon resumes (for example a gate script amends HEAD), the resumed rebase stage reuses the old commit's saved result and publishes the new commit without gating it. With today's local executor, an attached handle re-runs on the current tree, so only the saved-result path is exposed. A future remote executor would also return the old commit's result from a stored handle.",
   "reproduction": "unreproduced: needs a full engine restart harness with the checkout moved between checkpoints; judged from code",
   "evidence": "gate-execution.ts:20-23 `if (ctx.state.gateResults?.stage !== stage || ...round !== round) ctx.state.gateResults = { stage, round, sha: await headSha(cwd), values: {} }; ... if (results[purpose]) return results[purpose];` The stored sha is never compared with the current head. Lines 25-28 pick the stored handle by stage, round and purpose only. In mergeForDelivery (engine.ts:2381-2396), a resume skips completeMerge when head != before and calls runGateExecution('rebase'). Nothing pins the head there. In normal operation nothing moves HEAD between the checkpoint and the resume (prepareMerge returns early and checkoutCommitted resets to HEAD). So it takes a gate or an outside actor moving HEAD, which base also didn't guard during an uninterrupted run."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A checkout changes while the daemon is stopped during post-merge checks. After restarting, the factory can accept the newer commit using the previous commit's passing results.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"$TMPDIR/gate-adjudication-sjk6iy4h/probe.ts\"",
    "output": "F1 {\"cached\":{\"currentSha\":\"M2\",\"recordedSha\":\"M1\",\"starts\":1,\"attaches\":1},\"pending\":{\"starts\":0,\"attaches\":1,\"currentSha\":\"M2\"}}"
   },
   "evidence": "The isolated probe mocked headSha and injected an executor; it reproduced both reuse mechanisms, not publication. HEAD returns `results[purpose]` immediately and selects a pending handle using only stage, round and purpose. Neither path compares commits. Delivery's validateMerge checks parents, not equality with the tested commit, and its rebase checks lack the ordinary gate-evidence SHA guard. At base, mergeForDelivery called runGates afresh rather than reusing persisted results."
  }
 },
